|~ `::holds`, the kind of an invariant, and the laws declared under it.
   ~|

:holds
  |~~ The kind of an invariant, a query that the values of a label, the
      args of a word, a part of them or the answer of a word keeps,
      declared as a definition under the name it holds and named by the
      refusal of a value that breaks it, `:Small/TooLargeError ::holds~(lt
      10)`: the value is checked when it is built, read or answered, and
      refused under that name when the query answers false.
      ::link~(::qlang/verbs | doc)
  ~~|

:holds/refusesUnderItsName
  |~~ A value that breaks an invariant is refused under its name. ~~|
  ::law~(:Small |~~ Below ten. ~~| | :Small/TooLargeError ::holds~(lt 10) | [(::Small(3) | type) (::Small(12) !| type)] | eq [::Small ::Small/TooLargeError])
